Subject: [PATCH] dwc2: verbose role-switch and host bring-up instrumentation
Upstream-Status: Pending

Diagnostics for catplay-firmware issue #1: on some head units the dongle
switches to USB host mode after an iAP2/CarPlay role-switch request and
then never sees an accessory for the full 5s probe window. Almost every
interesting transition in that path logs at dev_dbg/dev_vdbg, so a normal
capture shows nothing and the two candidate explanations cannot be told
apart:

 a) the root hub was never activated - dwc2_core_host_init() never applied
    HPRT0_PWR, so the port is unpowered and nothing can attach; or
 b) the port is live but the head unit never re-presents itself.

This patch is the single place where all of that instrumentation lives, so
it can be dropped or carried as one unit. It consolidates what used to be
spread over four patches (the logging half of the old
0022-dwc2-remove-3x100ms-overhead..., plus 0023, 0038 and 0041) and adds
HPRT0 coverage, which was missing entirely - not one dwc2 log line read
that register.

What it covers:

 * drd.c - the requested role and phy_mode, the dwc2_ovr_avalid()/
   dwc2_ovr_bvalid() return values, and a one-shot dump of
   GSNPSID/GHWCFG4/GOTGCTL at drd init. The last one answers whether
   GOTGCTL_DBNCE_FLTR_BYPASS (which dwc2_ovr_gotgctl() sets on every
   override write) is honoured by this core at all; in captured dumps it
   always reads back as 0, which decides whether the ~100ms IDDIG debounce
   in dwc2_core_reset() is avoidable.

 * core.c - full register state (GOTGCTL/GUSBCFG/GINTSTS/GINTMSK/GRSTCTL)
   around dwc2_force_mode() and at start/success/timeout of
   dwc2_wait_for_mode(), with elapsed milliseconds. This is what makes the
   two racing wait_for_mode() calls visible (see patch 0039).

 * gadget.c - dwc2_hsotg_core_connect() refusing to clear DCTL_SFTDISCON
   because BSESVLD never arrived. Expected to be set immediately or shortly
   after via interrupt; if the PHY is misconfigured it never comes, and
   that used to be silent.

 * hcd_intr.c - port connect/enable/overcurrent interrupts, i.e. whether
   *any* electrical port activity happens during the probe window.

 * hcd.c - dwc2_conn_id_status_change() entry/branch/hand-off,
   dwc2_hcd_start(), dwc2_core_host_init()'s port-power decision (including
   a warning when op_state is not OTG_STATE_A_HOST, which silently skips
   HPRT0_PWR), and _dwc2_hcd_start()'s HPRT0/vbus-supply/root-hub-resume
   results.

 * hcd.c - a bounded HPRT0 sampler (250ms x 24 = 6s) started once the root
   hub has been activated, decoding PWR/CONNSTS/CONNDET/ENA/SUSP/OVRCURR
   plus line state and speed.

 * phy-ingenic-usb.c - what the PHY was actually told on every role switch:
   USBRDT before/after with IDDIG_EN/IDDIG_REG decoded, plus USBPCR and
   USBPCR1 (USB_MODE, the VBUS/session overrides, the D+/D- pulldowns).
   Since 0019 the role is selected purely through the IDDIG override and
   USBPCR is never written again, so this is the only way to see whether the
   PHY and the controller agree about the current role - CONFIG_DEVMEM is
   off in this config, so these registers cannot be read from userspace.

Diagnostics only - no behavioural change.

